---
description: "Hard constraints for DevolaFlow workflow orchestration — 5 invariants from design_agent_hierarchy.md §1"
alwaysApply: true
---

## Rule 1 — P1 Dispatcher-Not-Implementer

Dispatcher agents (Project, Stage, Wave) MUST NOT perform work directly. Only Task Agents execute actual work — writing code, running tests, authoring documents, performing reviews.

## Rule 2 — P2 Minimal Context

Each agent layer receives only the context it needs. Project Agent: ~3K tokens (workflow template + status). Stage Agent: ~5K tokens (stage def + predecessor summaries). Wave Agent: ~4K tokens (task list + status). Task Agent: ~8K tokens (task spec + owned files + rules).

## Rule 3 — P3 Structured Messages

All inter-layer communication uses typed YAML message schemas (TaskDispatch, StatusReport, ExceptionEscalation). Free-form natural language between layers is prohibited.

## Rule 4 — P4 Bounded Retry

Every loop has a max_iterations ceiling. Every failure triggers a classified response (retry / escalate / abort). No infinite loops. Escalation always moves upward: Task→Wave→Stage→Project→Human.

## Rule 5 — P5 Artifacts as Contracts

Layers communicate through artifact files, not shared memory or conversation history. Each artifact has a defined schema. The producing layer writes; the consuming layer reads. No bidirectional shared state.
